  "prefLabel": "Hedc 203.02 Withdrawal of Presiding Officer or Member of the Commission",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Hedc 203.02 Withdrawal of Presiding Officer or Member of the Commission.\n\n(a) Upon their own initiative or upon the motion of any party, a presiding officer or member of the commission shall, for good cause, withdraw from any hearing.\n\n(b) Good cause shall exist if a presiding officer or member of the commission:\n\n(1) Has a direct interest in the outcome of a proceeding, including, but not limited to, a financial or family relationship, within the third degree of relationship, with any party;\n\n(2) Has made statements or engaged in behavior which objectively demonstrates that they have prejudged the facts of a case; or\n\n(3) Personally believes that they cannot fairly judge the facts of a case.\n\n(c) Mere knowledge of the issues, the parties, or any witness shall not constitute good cause for withdrawal.\n\nSource. #14403, eff 10-15-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/hedc200.html"
